NAME
     uname - what this system is

SYNOPSIS
     uname [-a] [-s] [-n] [-r] [-v] [-m] [-o]

DESCRIPTION
     uname prints the system's name, and with options the rest of what
     it says about itself.

OPTIONS
     -s   the kernel's name
     -n   this machine's name
     -r   the release
     -v   the version, which says when it was built
     -m   the machine (riscv64)
     -o   the operating system
     -a   all of it

SEE ALSO
     hostname(1), dmesg(1)
